        <briefdescription>
<para>Add the rows of node <computeroutput>A</computeroutput> to a matrix of a particle: <formula id="181">$ \boldsymbol{K}_{AB} $</formula> for all nodes <formula id="170">$ B $</formula>, from the derivatives of the force of the node (<ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_stiffness_of_node" kindref="compound">StiffnessOfNode</ref>) and the trial shape functions at the evaluation point. computePhysicsKernels() of a particle forms its tangent this way, from the stiffness of each node and its inertia. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nDim</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Spatial dimension. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nDofPerNode</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Number of degrees of freedom per node. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">ofNode</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The derivatives of the force of node <computeroutput>A</computeroutput> with respect to the interpolated increment (in computePhysicsKernels() with its inertia). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">A</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The node. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">N</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The trial shape functions <formula id="71">$ N_B $</formula>, 1 x nNodes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">dN_dY</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Their gradients <formula id="182">$ \partial N_B / \partial Y_l $</formula>, nDim x nNodes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">d2N_dYdY</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Their second gradients, nDim^2 x nNodes, entry <formula id="183">$ (l\, n_{\text{dim}} + m, B) $</formula> is <formula id="176">$ \partial^2 N_B / \partial Y_l \partial Y_m $</formula>; empty for a particle without second gradients. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">K</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The matrix, column-major, (nNodes nDofPerNode) x (nNodes nDofPerNode); the rows are added. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
