        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void Marmot::Discretizations::Meshfree::addBoundOfAbsoluteStiffnessTimes</definition>
        <argsstring>(Particle &amp;particle, const double *columnWeights, int nColumns, double *bound, double timeNew, double dT)</argsstring>
        <name>addBoundOfAbsoluteStiffnessTimes</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::Discretizations::Meshfree::addBoundOfAbsoluteStiffnessTimes</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_particle" kindref="compound">Particle</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>particle</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const double *</type>
          <declname>columnWeights</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>nColumns</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>double *</type>
          <declname>bound</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>double</type>
          <declname>timeNew</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>double</type>
          <declname>dT</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Add an upper bound of <formula id="78">$ |\boldsymbol{K}|\, \boldsymbol{W} $</formula>, the absolute value of a particle&apos;s stiffness times nonnegative weights, without forming the stiffness (<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_absolute_stiffness_bound" kindref="compound">AbsoluteStiffnessBound</ref>, which the particle describes its stiffness to; see <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_particle_1aab0d22df342729365537585c8b3a6517" kindref="member">Particle::describeStiffness()</ref> for the state it is of). The particle is left as it was found. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The bound a host needs for the critical time step of an explicit scheme, e.g. by the Collatz-Wielandt bound of the mass-scaled stiffness, which needs <formula id="221">$ |\boldsymbol{K}|\boldsymbol{w} $</formula> only. It costs O(nodes) instead of the O(nodes^2) of the stiffness. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">particle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The particle (<ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_particle_1aab0d22df342729365537585c8b3a6517" kindref="member">Particle::describeStiffness()</ref>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">columnWeights</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The nonnegative weights <formula id="222">$ \boldsymbol{W} $</formula>, column-major, nDof x nColumns, in the dof order of the particle. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">nColumns</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The number of columns of <computeroutput>columnWeights</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">bound</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Column-major, nDof x nColumns: the bound is added. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">timeNew</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The time of the zero increment the stiffness is evaluated with. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">dT</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The time increment of the zero increment. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::invalid_argument</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>for a particle of a dimension other than 2 or 3, or with more than maxDofsPerNode dofs per node; std::runtime_error from a particle that does not describe its stiffness. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
